LumOn - World-Probe Tracing and Surface Cache Lighting:

  Goal:
  Trace geometry independently of lighting readiness; resolve surface hits from the Surface Cache,
  distinguish sky from incomplete traces, and prevent unresolved work from starving publication.

  References:
  - docs/LumOn.SurfaceCache.LightingContract.md
  - docs/LumOn.TraceSceneGeometryContract.md
  - docs/LumOn.WorldProbeLighting.ArchitectureAndIssues.md

  Tasks:
  ✔ Diagnose the live Surface Cache readiness failure. Expose capture, direct-seed, and publication
    failure reasons; establish which condition prevents the first ready page before changing policy.
    - Diagnosed: prerequisite status and cumulative capture/seed/indirect/combine failure counters
      are exposed in runtime self-checks and periodic "[VGE] Surface cache readiness:" log entries.
      GPU rejection counters identify the failing operation, not the exact failing texel or input.
      Live run: all 24,948 captures failed; 38 pages awaited capture and no seed work started.
      Terrain feedback collapsed to slot 0. The terrain shader reads slot mapping from
      VgeLumonSceneChunkSlotParamsUBO, but its hook only uploaded obsolete standalone uniforms.
      Added the missing owned UBO and per-use binding restoration. The GPU regression maps to slot 232;
      removing only the new binding reproduces slot 0 with generation 0 while preserving the patch ID.
      Post-fix in-game publication remains to be verified under the live-validation task below.
  ✔ Correct temporal reprojection in lumon_velocity.fsh and lumon_debug_temporal.glsl: convert
    current render-relative positions into the previous render-origin space before projection.
    Validate translation, rotation, camera bob, and the dependent lumon_probe_atlas_temporal history.
    - Both renderers now pair committed view-projection matrices with their render origins and
      upload the previous matrix composed with the current-to-previous origin translation.
      Origin subtraction uses double precision; the full view transform retains camera bob.
    - Fresh build and all 29 focused tests passed: origin lifecycle and perspective (3), velocity
      translation/rotation/bob and invalid history (6), normal/debug renderer uploads (2), imported
      debug reprojection (1), and dependent probe-atlas temporal behavior (17). No tests skipped.
      In-game visual confirmation remains under the live-validation task below.
  ✔ Correct eye-relative view direction and distance in vge_parallax.glsl and vge_normaldepth.glsl.
    Account for the eye offset in the view matrix; validate parallax and normal-map fading with
    camera bob and camera offsets, without applying view translation twice.
    - Shared terrain view helper derives the eye from the existing draw's rigid modelViewMatrix.
      POM direction, POM distance fade, and normal-map distance fade use that same eye-relative
      vector. Surface positions remain render-relative and tangent frames remain in world axes.
    - Fresh build: 32 focused tests passed, including three imported GPU material regressions;
      one existing TinyTokenizer insertion test remains explicitly skipped. Verified shared
      vertex/fragment matrix linkage, rotation/bob offsets, POM displacement and normal fading.
      Full installed terrain variants and in-game visual behavior remain live-validation work.
  ✔ Make terrain PatchId and chunk-slot selection use the same inward-biased owning block in
    VanillaShaderPatches.cs and lumonscene_patchid.glsl. Validate all six faces at positive and
    negative chunk boundaries, including capture and sampling of the selected surface.
    - Patch mapping now returns its inward-biased absolute owning block. Terrain slot lookup uses
      that same block shifted by 5, preserving floor semantics at negative chunk boundaries.
      Patch-local integer layout arithmetic uses shifts for power-of-two scaling.
    - GPU regression executes the injected terrain mapping at all six faces on positive and negative
      chunk boundaries, with fractional camera motion and chunk crossings. Its actual slot/patch/UV
      feed voxel capture; sampling checks distinct materials on opposite sides of each boundary.
    - Fresh build: all 23 focused tests passed, none skipped. Restoring the old slot calculation
      inside the test failed all six positive-face boundary cases while eight controls passed.
      In-game visual confirmation remains under the live-validation task below.
  ☐ Remove vanilla GetLightRGBs and neighboring-light availability dependencies from world-probe
    geometry tracing when hit lighting is deferred to the Surface Cache.
  ☐ Separate surface hits, established sky visibility, distance/budget exhaustion, and unavailable
    geometry. Define distant-light completion explicitly; do not turn incomplete traces into sky.
  ☐ Add Surface Cache indirect sky/distant-light completion using those outcomes. Reconcile it with
    the existing vanilla sunlight seed to avoid double-counting; retain retries for missing data.
  ☐ Preserve valid world-probe directional samples while retrying unresolved cache hits, with bounded
    work, per-direction validity, and generation-safe history so missing samples cannot publish light.
  ☐ Fix the confirmed initial-readiness blocker and prevent whole-page retry starvation, preserving
    valid progress without publishing uncaptured or uninitialized texels.
  ☐ Validate through subagent-run focused tests: missing cache, unavailable geometry, distance limits,
    sky openings, mixed ready/unready hits, movement, streaming, edits, and resource recreation.
  ☐ Verify in-game: first cache publication, continuing probe traces/updates, sealed-room darkness,
    and sky through an opening. Report live evidence separately from controlled test results.

  Constraints:
  Keep geometry tracing independent of cache readiness (already implemented; preserve regression coverage).
  Use integer shifts for power-of-two scaling where equivalent, preserving overflow behavior.
  Initial direct-seed publication must not depend on indirect convergence or ready world probes.
